// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch20 U06 the release: Ethren. Corran's face (the veil fell mid-fight). He tells her he
// heard every visit. She tells him she's not coming back to the Sanctum anymore. If ch13_corran_house: someone else
// lives in their house now, and that's all right. If ch13_camp_talk: Asha stands BEHIND her, not beside. The copper ring
// (the keepsake) is the last thing to fade. The widow's goodbye she refused for twenty-four years.
title: ch20_ethren_release
location: ch20/undertow_layers
---
@letterbox on
@camera U25
@music silence fade=1.0
<<if $ch13_camp_talk>>
    @mark asha behind_ysolde walk
<<endif>>
Ethren as "Corran" [tender]: I heard you. Every visit. Every one. #line:ch20_ethren_001 #tn:"Ethren speaks as Corran Ysel, Ysolde's husband: patient, funny, gentle."
@wait 3.0
Ysolde [grief]: I'm not coming back to the Sanctum. Not anymore. #line:ch20_ethren_002
<<if $ch13_corran_house>>
    @wait 2.0
    Ysolde [sad]: Someone else lives in our house now. A family. They kept the step clean. #line:ch20_ethren_003
    Ysolde [tender]: It's all right. #line:ch20_ethren_004
<<endif>>
@wait 2.0
Ethren as "Corran" [soft_smile]: Good. Go and be somewhere else. #line:ch20_ethren_005
@music release_sting fade=0.0
@vfx glimmer_lift at=ethren count=40 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 8.0
@camera U26
@vfx glimmer_lift at=copper_ring count=1 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 5.0
<<set $ch20_ethren_released = true>>
@letterbox off
===
